dioxus-primitives and dioxus-attributes from https://github.com/DioxusLabs/components at
revision 9a758255ea26e2b20c8cecf4c1c946feb9e71da7 (MIT or Apache-2.0 at your option,
LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE here), ported to Dioxus 0.8.0-alpha.3: named keys are
Key::Named(NamedKey::..), Key and ClientPoint come from dioxus::html, VNode::key is a
method, the attributes! macro takes the boxed slice 0.8 renders event handlers as, the
navbar adds its listeners through attributes!, and the toast provider fills ToastProps
itself. The manifests name their dependency versions instead of a workspace. The preview
and test harness are not here.

Two changes of behaviour for Blitz, which makes no click out of Enter or Space on a button:
the select trigger and the tab trigger open or select on those keys themselves (marked
"(yakin)" in the source).
A third: use_animated_open hides a closed element at once instead of awaiting its exit
animation through document::eval, which does nothing under Blitz and left the closed select
list in the DOM as an unseen tab stop.
A fourth: the select trigger takes the focus back when its list closes; Blitz drops the focus
with the list's element and the next Tab would start over from the top of the page.
